sglang-sxm2
===========

An agentic-coding inference engine for V100 GPUs, based on SGLang.

    SGLang -- the inference engine
    https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
    Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

This project incorporates work from:

    sglang-V100 -- the original Volta (sm70) port of SGLang
    https://github.com/haohervchb/sglang-V100
    Parts of the sm70 kernels, the Qwen4-Exp model support and the serving
    recipes carried here originate in that repository.
    Related: https://github.com/haohervchb/flashinfer (sm70 FlashInfer)
             https://github.com/haohervchb/GooseLLM (TileLang FlashAttention
             and GDN kernels for V100, Apache 2.0)

    1Cat-vLLM -- vLLM for V100; source of the sm70 TurboMind block-FP8 and
    FP16 MoE backend the build compiles
    https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM

This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
supported by the SGLang project or LMSYS. Please do not file issues about this
project's sm70 code against upstream SGLang, and do not file issues about
upstream SGLang here.

Third-party components
----------------------

The Volta build links against, derives from, or adapts code from the following
projects. Each remains under its own license and copyright; consult each
project for terms. Unless noted, they are not redistributed in this repository;
the installer fetches them at pinned revisions.

  lmdeploy / TurboMind -- sm70 MoE and FP8 GEMM kernels (via 1Cat-vLLM)
    https://github.com/InternLM/lmdeploy
    Apache License 2.0

  marlin_v100 -- SM70 Marlin GPTQ/AWQ kernels
    https://github.com/zhinianqin/marlin_v100

  flash-attention-v100 -- FlashAttention for V100
    https://github.com/ai-bond/flash-attention-v100
    BSD 3-Clause License

  v100-skinny -- the QPN8 FP8 decode GEMV adapted in
    python/sglang/kernels/jit/csrc/sm70_fp8_qpn8_decode.cu
    https://github.com/dnv2003/v100-skinny
    MIT License

  NVIDIA CUTLASS
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass
    Copyright (c) NVIDIA Corporation

  FlashInfer (patched for sm70; see patches/flashinfer-sm70.patch)
    https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer

  TileLang -- the sm70 attention and GDN kernels build on TileLang
    https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang

Patches under patches/ are modifications to the above projects, distributed
